.$\n\n$\\,y(1)≈$\n{{field-1}},\n$\\,z(1)≈$\n{{field-2}},\n$\\,w(1)≈$\n{{field-3}}" 13194139534967 true] [17592186323354 1113 #uuid "04ed6984-51d2-56a0-9687-075ebc560f1e" 13194139534967 true] [17592186323354 1145 "Euler's method approximates the solution of an initial value problem containing a system of ODEs by applying the update rule component-wise to each equation.\n\nSince we want to find the value of $y$, $z$ and $w$ at $x=1,$ we will use a step size of\n\n$$\nΔx=1-0=1.\n$$\n\nFirst, we place the initial condition data in a table.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ | $w$ | ${w}^{′}$ | $Δw$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $2$ |  |  | $1$ |  |  | $1$ |  |  |\n\nNext, we compute ${y}^{′},$ ${z}^{′},$ and ${w}^{′}$ according to the given rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\sqrt[3]{x+y-1}+z \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{0+2-1}+1 \\\\  & =2 \\\\ {z}^{′} & =\\frac{{y}^{2}-1}{w+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{2}-1}{1+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ {w}^{′} & =\\sqrt{x+{z}^{2}}-y \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+{1}^{2}}-2 \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add these to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ | $w$ | ${w}^{′}$ | $Δw$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $2$ | $2$ |  | $1$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ |  | $1$ | $-1$ |  |\n\nNext, we compute $Δy,$ $Δz,$ and $Δw$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2 \\\\ Δz & ={z}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ Δw & ={w}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add these to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ | $w$ | ${w}^{′}$ | $Δw$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $2$ | $2$ | $2$ | $1$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $-1$ |\n\nTo get the new values of $x,$ $y,$ $z,$ and $w$ in the *next* row, we add $Δx$ to $x,$ $Δy$ to $y,$ $Δz$ to $z,$ and $Δw$ to $w,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=0+1=1 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=2+2=4 \\\\ {z}_{\\text{new}} & =z+Δz=1+\\frac{3}{2}=\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ {w}_{\\text{new}} & =w+Δw=1+(-1)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these values to our table in a new row gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ | $w$ | ${w}^{′}$ | $Δw$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $2$ | $2$ | $2$ | $1$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $-1$ |\n| $1$ | $4$ |  |  | $\\frac{5}{2}$ |  |  | $0$ |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n$y(1)≈4,$\n$z(1)≈\\frac{5}{2},$\nand\n$w(1)≈0.$" 13194139534967 true] [17592186323355 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323356 13194139534967 true] [17592186323355 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323357 13194139534967 true] [17592186323355 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534967 true] [17592186323355 1041 "field-1" 13194139534967 true] [17592186323355 1104 #edb/ref 17592186323357 13194139534967 true] [17592186323355 1110 #uuid "93ec7bc9-2dcc-5eb7-a98a-2823f9c1aab7" 13194139534967 true] [17592186323356 1034 "2" 13194139534967 true] [17592186323356 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534967 true] [17592186323356 1111 #uuid "29ba91c8-0828-5691-881e-8b0ce5e6bef6" 13194139534967 true] [17592186323357 1034 "4" 13194139534967 true] [17592186323357 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534967 true] [17592186323357 1111 #uuid "a8737bbc-2a6f-53b8-866e-aa7cb3f1076e" 13194139534967 true] [17592186323358 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323359 13194139534967 true] [17592186323358 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534967 true] [17592186323358 1041 "field-2" 13194139534967 true] [17592186323358 1104 #edb/ref 17592186323359 13194139534967 true] [17592186323358 1110 #uuid "b402eacb-5d9a-5b1a-80b0-04f8231fc3e8" 13194139534967 true] [17592186323359 1034 "\\frac{5}{2}" 13194139534967 true] [17592186323359 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534967 true] [1759